1
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:43,500
Beyond the horizon lies the secret to a new beginning.

2
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:21,000
Waterworld is a adventure, action, science fiction
film directed by Kevin Reynolds.

3
00:16:52,500 --> 00:16:58,500
In a futuristic world where the polar ice caps have melted and made Earth a liquid planet, a
beautiful barmaid rescues a mutant seafarer from a floating island prison.

4
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:36,000
They escape, along with her young charge, Enola, and sail off aboard his ship.

5
00:28:07,500 --> 00:28:13,500
But the trio soon becomes the target of a menacing pirate who covets
the map to 'Dryland'—which is tattooed on Enola's back.

6
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:51,000
Mariner, played by Kevin Costner.

7
00:39:22,500 --> 00:39:28,500
Deacon, played by Dennis Hopper.

8
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Helen, played by Jeanne Tripplehorn.

9
00:50:37,500 --> 00:50:43,500
Enola, played by Tina Majorino.

10
00:56:15,000 --> 00:56:21,000
Enforcer, played by R. D. Call.

11
01:01:52,500 --> 01:01:58,500
Nord, played by Gerard Murphy.

12
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
Waterworld is a 1995 American post-apocalyptic action film, directed by
Kevin Reynolds and co-written by Peter Rader and David Twohy.

13
01:13:07,500 --> 01:13:13,500
It was based on Rader's original 1986 screenplay and stars Kevin Costner,
who also produced it with Charles Gordon and John Davis.

14
01:18:45,000 --> 01:18:51,000
It was distributed by Universal Pictures.

15
01:24:22,500 --> 01:24:28,500
The setting of the film is in the distant future.

16
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
The polar ice caps have completely melted, and the sea level has risen
over 7,600 m (25,000 ft), covering nearly all of the land.

17
01:35:37,500 --> 01:35:43,500
The plot of the film centers on a nameless antihero, "The Mariner"
(Costner), a drifter who sails the Earth in his trimaran.

18
01:41:15,000 --> 01:41:21,000
The most expensive film ever made at the time, Waterworld was released to mixed reviews from critics, who praised the
futuristic setting and premise but criticized the execution, including the characterization and acting performances.

19
01:46:52,500 --> 01:46:58,500
The film also was unable to recoup its massive budget at the box office despite being the ninth highest-grossing film
of 1995; however, the film did later become profitable owing to video and other post-cinema sales.

20
01:52:30,000 --> 01:52:36,000
The film was nominated for an Academy Award in the
category Best Sound at the 68th Academy Awards.

21
01:58:07,500 --> 01:58:13,500
The film's release was accompanied by a novelization, video games, and four themed attractions at Universal Studios
Hollywood, Universal Studios Singapore, Universal Studios Japan, and Universal Studios Beijing called WaterWorld.

22
02:03:45,000 --> 02:03:51,000
The film explores themes of sailboat, human evolution, tattoo, ocean, mutant.

23
02:09:22,500 --> 02:09:28,500
The tone is thought_provoking.
